From 69b1f5d67fb6cb06d0f0e8879f813244c7b5dad4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:16:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix: iPhone home-screen app was treated as an in-app browser

iOS home-screen apps send a user agent without 'Safari/', so inAppBrowser() was true and 'Continue
with Google' showed the old 'Open in Safari / copy link' sheet instead of starting the hand-off.
Home-screen apps are now excluded. The waiting sheet and the Safari page both show a check code,
the sheet shows when it last checked and has an 'I've signed in' button, and the server logs
create/redeem so problems show in Firebase > Functions > Logs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CEydp1FfcQQGxK6fMzr743
